  "id": "V027",
  "description": "A cycle with no Condorcet winner is resolved by rung 1, Copeland score: most pairwise victories wins even though that movie lost a head-to-head",
  "spec_clause": "Phase 2 / Tally: 'Cycles are possible (A beats B beats C beats A) and must be handled rather than left to crash. Resolve in order: 1 Copeland score, 2 Approval count, 3 Rotation fairness, 4 Shortest runtime, 5 Seeded random.'",
  "rationale": "5 attendees, 4 finalists. Phase 1: m1 5 rows/5 yes -> approval 1.00; m2 5 rows/4 yes -> 0.80; m3 5 rows/3 yes -> 0.60; m4 4 rows/3 yes -> coverage 4/5 = 0.80, approval 0.75. All eligible, all clear the floor, all four fit in N_FINALISTS = 5. Ranking by yes-votes: m1 (5), m2 (4), then m3 and m4 tie on 3 and the tie is resolved by approval (m4 0.75 > m3 0.60), giving m1, m2, m4, m3. Round robin, 6 pairs: m1>m2 3-2; m1>m3 4-1; m4>m1 3-2; m2 vs m3 2-2 with one explicit no preference -> tie, no winner; m2>m4 3-2; m3>m4 3-2. There is a cycle m1 > m2 > m4 > m1, so no finalist beats every other and there is no Condorcet winner. Rung 1 Copeland: m1 = 2 (m2, m3), m2 = 1 (m4), m3 = 1 (m4), m4 = 1 (m1). Unique maximum m1 = 2 -> m1 wins by Copeland; no lower rung is consulted.",
